Krill's Loader, repository version 194, built for this project.

    make prg PLATFORM=c64 VERSION=194 PROJECT=c64fps \
             EXTCONFIGPATH=<this dir> INSTALL=0400 RESIDENT=8000 ZP=e8

loaderconfig.inc is ours; everything else here is Krill's output. Prerequisites are ca65/ld65
(cc65), make and perl -- NOT acme, whatever the Makefile's zip list suggests. On macOS the
build needs VERSION= passed by hand, because the Makefile derives it with `grep -oP`, which
BSD grep does not have, and an empty VERSION makes the symbol step fail after the binaries
have already assembled fine.

WHY THIS CONFIG (measured, resident size at each step):
    bare load-raw                  225 B
    + NTSC_COMPATIBILITY           226 B   +1, and we are NTSC -- the prebuilts have it OFF
    + LOAD_VIA_KERNAL_FALLBACK     531 B   +305, and it is what makes the disk work on a
                                           stock VICE and a real C64 with no settings changed
    + LOAD_UNDER_D000_DFFF         647 B   +116, lands IHOL under the I/O hole directly
                                           instead of via $c000 and a hand-written copy

